📗 User Guide

Operating System: Rocky Linux 10
Application Name: Process Monitoring & Visualization Tool
Execution Method: GUI-based (Python)

1. Introduction

This tool provides an easy-to-use graphical interface for monitoring running processes on your Linux system.
It displays key information such as:

PID

User

Memory usage

Elapsed time

Parent PID

Executable path

Command line

Designed for clarity and simplicity, the application is suitable for both developers and system operators.

2. How to Run the Application
Requirements

Before running the tool, ensure the system has:

Python 3.9 or higher

Basic GUI support

Execute permission for the parsing script

Start the Application

To launch the program, run:

python3 gui.py


There is no need to run any other script manually.
The GUI automatically retrieves data from the system.

3. Main Window Overview

When the application starts, the main window displays a table containing process information.
Each row represents one running process on the system.

Displayed Columns

The table includes the following fields:

Field	Description
Elapsed Time	How long the process has been running
PID	Process ID
User	Owner of the process
Memory (kB)	Memory usage in kilobytes
Memory (%)	Percentage of total system memory used
PPID	Parent Process ID
Path	Executable file location
Command Line	Full command used to start the process
4. Refreshing Data

The GUI automatically retrieves updated process information each time you press the Refresh button (if provided).
This allows you to monitor changes in real time.

5. Sorting and Navigation (If enabled)

Depending on the GUI version, you may sort rows by clicking column headers such as:

PID

User

Memory usage

Elapsed time

This helps when locating processes of interest.

6. Error Handling

If the system cannot retrieve certain information (e.g., missing executable path), the application will show:

[Unknown]


This is normal behavior and does not indicate a failure.

The GUI will continue operating even if some process entries contain incomplete data.

7. Closing the Application

To exit, simply close the window using your desktop environment’s standard close button.
No additional cleanup is required.

8. Notes

The tool only reads system information and does not modify or terminate processes.

Administrator privileges are not required, unless restricted by system security policies.

Designed specifically for Rocky Linux 10, but may operate on similar Linux distributions.

9. Support

If you encounter issues or need enhancements, please contact your system administrator or development team.
